course: dictionary
lesson: 14591
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «plotted» is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning is right. «We plotted the points on the graph» is about maths, because points and graphs go together.
explain: «The gang plotted to rob the bank» means something different. Plotted here means secretly planned something, usually something bad. The words secretly and rob are your clues. «The writer plotted the story carefully» means planned the story of a book, so the story has events that fit together.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it? Try each meaning in the sentence, and see which one still makes sense.
fact: Plotted is the past form of plot, so it tells you something that has already happened.
fact: «Plotted» can mean marked points on a graph, grid or map.
fact: «Plotted» can mean secretly planned something, usually something bad.
fact: «Plotted» can mean planned the story of a book or film, as in «a well-plotted mystery».
fact: In history, Guy Fawkes and others plotted to blow up Parliament in 1605. This is called the Gunpowder Plot.
exercise: «We plotted the points on the grid and joined them to make a line.» What does plotted mean here? | Secretly planned something bad | *Marked points on a grid | Planted in a pot | Planned the story of a book
exercise: «The villains plotted to steal the royal jewels at midnight.» What does plotted mean here? | Potted in a plant pot | Marked points on a map | *Secretly planned something bad | Planned the story of a film
exercise: «The film had a well-plotted mystery, with every clue fitting together.» What does well-plotted mean? | Drawn on a map | *Planned so the events fit together | Hidden under the bed | Painted in bright colours
test: «Mia plotted the temperatures on a graph for science.» What does plotted mean? | Secretly planned something | Planned the story of a book | Planted in a pot | *Marked points on a graph
test: «The gang plotted to rob the bank.» What does plotted mean? | Potted a plant | Planned the story of a film | Marked points on a map | *Secretly planned something, usually bad
exam: Ben says «plotted» always means secretly planned something bad. Is he right? | Yes, it always means something bad | No, it means painted | *No, it can also mean marked points on a graph or planned a story | Yes, because plotted is a noun
